relic-toolkit
------------------------------------------
RELIC is a modern cryptographic meta-toolkit with emphasis on efficiency and
flexibility. RELIC can be used to build efficient and usable cryptographic
toolkits tailored for specific security levels and algorithmic choices.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgmp10-6.3.0-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  librelic-devel-0.7.0-1bl1
  librelic0-0.7.0-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libgmp-devel-6.3.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/relic-toolkit/relic

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/relic-toolkit/relic/archive/0.7.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack relic-toolkit-0.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./relic-toolkit-0.7.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/relic-toolkit-0.7.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/relic-toolkit-0.7.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/librelic0-0.7.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/librelic-devel-0.7.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

